WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:07.750
Speaker 1: Republican Senator Mike Braun yesterday
said he would be OK putting the issue of interracial

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:15.039
marriage back to the states rather than the
Supreme Court decision, which bans bans on

00:00:15.039 --> 00:00:16.750
interracial marriage holding.

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:22.099
He would be fined, canceling that and letting
states decide Do you want interracial marriage

00:00:22.099 --> 00:00:26.710
to be legal or do you want interracial marriage
to be illegal?

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:31.289
This understandably created a firestorm because
it's a crazy thing to say.

00:00:31.289 --> 00:00:32.579
Let's look at the clip.

00:00:32.579 --> 00:00:36.039
Here is Mike Braun
Speaker 4: So you would be OK with the Supreme

00:00:36.039 --> 00:00:39.800
Court leaving the question of interracial
marriage to the states.

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:45.609
Speaker 2: Yes, I think that that's something
that if you're not wanting the Supreme Court

00:00:45.609 --> 00:00:50.829
to weigh in on issues like that, you're not
going to be able to have your cake and eat

00:00:50.829 --> 00:00:51.829
it too.

00:00:51.829 --> 00:00:52.829
I think that's hypocritical.

00:00:52.829 --> 00:00:56.030
Speaker 4: About Griswold versus Connecticut.

00:00:56.030 --> 00:01:01.829
You can list a whole host of issues, so
Speaker 1: he very clearly heard the question,

00:01:01.829 --> 00:01:08.430
and the point here is many Republicans like
Mike Braun like to say the Supreme Court really

00:01:08.430 --> 00:01:10.610
shouldn't decide about all sorts of things.

00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:15.320
The Supreme Court shouldn't decide that abortion,
generally speaking, should be legal.

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:16.560
It should just be up to the states.

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:22.151
The Supreme Court shouldn't decide that states
aren't allowed to ban same sex marriage, and

00:01:22.151 --> 00:01:27.780
so it's a reasonable question, which is would
you also apply to this to interracial marriage?

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:30.220
Should states be allowed to ban interracial
marriage?

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:32.590
He clearly heard the question and answered
it.

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:38.170
Unfortunately for him, this was a completely
outrageous thing to say, and he had to later

00:01:38.170 --> 00:01:40.850
walk it back, claiming he didn't hear the
question.

00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:46.939
Braun walks back remark, criticizing the Supreme
Court ruling that legalized interracial marriage,

00:01:46.939 --> 00:01:49.490
and you've got to go to the bottom of the
article on The Hill.

00:01:49.490 --> 00:01:55.390
In a statement to The Hill later Tuesday,
Braun said he misunderstood the question as

00:01:55.390 --> 00:01:56.390
posed.

00:01:56.390 --> 00:02:01.350
Earlier, during a virtual press conference,
I misunderstood a line of questioning that

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:04.280
ended up being about interracial marriage.

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:08.039
Let me be clear on that issue there is no
question the Constitution prohibits discrimination

00:02:08.039 --> 00:02:09.850
of any kind based on race.

00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:11.960
That is not something that is even up for
debate.

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:18.010
I condemn racism in any form, at all levels
and by any state's entities or individuals.

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:22.950
So claiming guilt, claiming he just didn't
even really know what what he was being asked

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:23.950
now.

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:31.500
There is a very important legal conversation
to have about when should states be left to

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:33.330
decide about whatever?

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:37.690
And not all of these issues are created equal
when you say, well, leave states to decide

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:38.690
about abortion.

00:02:38.690 --> 00:02:39.730
Well, OK.

00:02:39.730 --> 00:02:43.360
The Supreme Court put in place this undue
burden test.

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:46.280
That's the basis of Casey Casey is the court.

00:02:46.280 --> 00:02:49.030
The decision, in addition to Roe v. Wade.

00:02:49.030 --> 00:02:50.690
You've got Casey.

00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:56.910
And there the court put in place this undue
burden standard, which says that abortion

00:02:56.910 --> 00:03:05.650
restrictions are unconstitutional if the purpose
or effect places a substantial obstacle in

00:03:05.650 --> 00:03:09.250
the path of women who want to get an abortion.

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:15.600
So that that's one decision and one sort of
framework leaves states to decide about.

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:17.540
Do you have to have car insurance?

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:19.940
Most states say you do.

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:23.540
Virginia and New Hampshire have different
rules, like in New Hampshire.

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:31.200
Car insurance isn't mandatory, but if you're
driving causes damages, then you're liable.

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:34.410
And that's a decision that a state has made.

00:03:34.410 --> 00:03:39.690
Leave states to decide about should marijuana
be legal and can be purchased just like cigarets

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:40.690
or alcohol.

00:03:40.690 --> 00:03:44.190
Well, for now, states can decide about that.

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:51.860
If the federal government were to in some
way fully legalize marijuana.

00:03:51.860 --> 00:03:52.860
Reschedule it.

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:59.040
OK, then you would sort of have a fight when
it comes to the decision about interracial

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:00.340
marriage.

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:03.280
The Supreme Court said No, no, no, no, no.

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:07.870
There's a constitutional basis here, equal
the equal protection clause.

00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:16.190
If properly scrutinized as the Supreme Court
did, doesn't allow states to ban interracial

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:21.120
marriage, you can't leave it to the states
because of the federal supremacy clause and

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:25.580
the fact that banning interracial marriage
would violate the federal constitution.

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:28.520
So the framework is very different than some
of these other decisions.

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:35.670
So the point here is even if there is a legitimate
debate to be had about what should states

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:41.060
have to decide about interracial marriage
is outside of that, and I don't believe Mike

00:04:41.060 --> 00:04:43.161
Braun misheard it nor misunderstood it.

00:04:43.161 --> 00:04:44.910
I think he just gave the wrong answer.

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:47.630
It was just wrong and it was crazy.

00:04:47.630 --> 00:04:49.630
And he got called out for it and he had to
walk it back

